{"idx": 540, "prompt": "recommend how to name files (use of spaces or . - etc...)", "response": "When naming files, it's important to follow certain conventions to ensure that the file names are clear, descriptive, and compatible with various systems and applications. Here are some guidelines on how to name files, including considerations for spaces and other characters:\n\n### 1. Use Descriptive Names\nFile names should be descriptive and meaningful. They should clearly indicate the content of the file. Avoid generic names like \"file1,\" \"file2,\" etc.\n\n### 2. Avoid Spaces and Special Characters\nFile systems and many applications do not handle spaces and special characters well. Here are some best practices:\n\n- **Use Hyphens or Underscores**: Replace spaces with hyphens (-) or underscores (_). For example, \"document-title\" instead of \"document title.\"\n- **Avoid Special Characters**: Do not use special characters like `!`, `@`, `#`, `$`, `%`, `^`, `&`, `*`, `(`, `)`, `+`, `=`, `{`, `}`, `[`, `]`, `;`, `:`, `'`, `\"` (apostrophe), `,`, `<`, `>`, `/`, `\\`, `?`, `|`, `~`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `\u00b0`, `